Asha is standing near the door.
She smiles.
"Good night, Maya," Asha says.
"Good night, Asha," I say.
Asha goes outside.
I close the door.
It is completely quiet in the house now.
I come into the living room.
I sit on my comfortable sofa.
I look around in my new home.
Everything is kept in its right place.
The laptop is kept on the desk near the window.
The empty suitcase is lying under the bed.
The clothes are in the cupboard.
In the kitchen, the tea cups are kept on top of the shelf.
My flat is very beautiful.
I rest on the sofa and smile.
I feel very good here.
Now this is truly my home in Mumbai.
